{"type":"standard","title":"Patrick G. Halpin","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Patrick G. Halpin</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q7146535","titles":{"canonical":"Patrick_G._Halpin","normalized":"Patrick G. Halpin","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Patrick G. Halpin</span></span>"},"pageid":2911237,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b9/Patrick_Halpin_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":330,"height":440},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b9/Patrick_Halpin_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","width":330,"height":440},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1365696579","tid":"274c2866-86e9-11f1-ac78-1e325d07864e","timestamp":"2026-07-23T22:52:17Z","description":"American politician (born 1953)","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrick_G._Halpin","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrick_G._Halpin?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrick_G._Halpin?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Patrick_G._Halpin"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrick_G._Halpin","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Patrick_G._Halpin","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Patrick_G._Halpin?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Patrick_G._Halpin"}},"extract":"Patrick Goodchild Halpin is an American politician who served as the fifth county executive of Suffolk County, New York, from 1988 to 1991. Halpin succeeded Jim Gaughran as Chair of the Suffolk County Water Authority on December 18, 2018.","extract_html":"<p><b>Patrick Goodchild Halpin</b> is an American politician who served as the fifth county executive of Suffolk County, New York, from 1988 to 1991. Halpin succeeded Jim Gaughran as Chair of the Suffolk County Water Authority on December 18, 2018.</p>"}